    {
      "title": "Self-Loop Bottleneck Visualization",
      "description": "Compare self-loop counts between perfect and imperfect consonances. The 12:1 ratio is the categorical manifestation of the parallel fifths prohibition.",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0\"><title>Self-Loop Bottleneck</title><style>*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}body{font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0a0a1a;color:#e0e0e0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:30px}h1{font-size:1.4em;color:#7eb8ff;margin-bottom:5px}h2{font-size:.9em;font-weight:normal;color:#888;margin-bottom:30px}.chart-container{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:30px}.bar-group{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:8px}.bar-wrapper{width:70px;height:300px;background:#16163a;border-radius:8px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;overflow:hidden;position:relative;border:1px solid #2a2a5a}.bar{border-radius:6px 6px 0 0;transition:height .8s cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding-bottom:8px;font-weight:bold;font-size:1.2em}.bar-label{font-size:.85em;color:#ccc}.bar-type{font-size:.75em;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:10px;margin-top:2px}.explanation{max-width:650px;background:#16163a;border-radius:12px;padding:25px;border:1px solid #2a2a5a;line-height:1.6;font-size:.95em}.explanation h3{color:#7eb8ff;margin-bottom:10px}.explanation .highlight{color:#ff6b6b;font-weight:600}.explanation .highlight-g{color:#51cf66;font-weight:600}.anim-note{color:#666;font-size:.8em;margin-top:10px}</style></head><body><h1>The Self-Loop Bottleneck</h1><h2>Why parallel fifths are forbidden — in one picture</h2><div class=\"chart-container\"></div><div class=\"explanation\"><h3>What you're seeing</h3><p>A <strong>self-loop</strong> is a voice leading that starts and ends at the same interval. It represents all the ways two voices can move while maintaining their intervallic relationship.</p><p style=\"margin-top:10px\">For <span class=\"highlight-g\">imperfect consonances</span> (thirds and sixths), any parallel motion is allowed — both voices can move up by any amount and the interval stays consonant. That gives <strong>12 self-loops</strong> (one for each of the 12 possible step sizes in ZMod 12).</p><p style=\"margin-top:10px\">For <span class=\"highlight\">perfect consonances</span> (unison and perfect fifth), the parallel-motion prohibition eliminates 11 of these 12 self-loops. Only the <strong>identity</strong> (no motion at all) survives. The ratio is <strong>1:12</strong> — a 12-fold asymmetry.</p><p style=\"margin-top:10px\">This is <em>why</em> parallel fifths sound wrong: staying on a perfect fifth while moving is almost impossible under the rules. The mathematics forces composers away from perfect consonances.</p></div><script>const intervals=[{id:0,name:'Unison',short:'P1',perfect:true,loops:1},{id:3,name:'Minor 3rd',short:'m3',perfect:false,loops:12},{id:4,name:'Major 3rd',short:'M3',perfect:false,loops:12},{id:7,name:'Perfect 5th',short:'P5',perfect:true,loops:1},{id:8,name:'Minor 6th',short:'m6',perfect:false,loops:12},{id:9,name:'Major 6th',short:'M6',perfect:false,loops:12}];const container=document.querySelector('.chart-container');intervals.forEach((iv,i)=>{const group=document.createElement('div');group.className='bar-group';const wrapper=document.createElement('div');wrapper.className='bar-wrapper';const bar=document.createElement('div');bar.className='bar';bar.style.height='0%';bar.style.background=iv.perfect?'linear-gradient(to top,#cc4444,#ff8a8a)':'linear-gradient(to top,#2d8a4e,#6de08a)';bar.textContent=iv.loops;const label=document.createElement('div');label.className='bar-label';label.textContent=iv.name;const type=document.createElement('div');type.className='bar-type';type.style.background=iv.perfect?'rgba(255,107,107,0.2)':'rgba(81,207,102,0.2)';type.style.color=iv.perfect?'#ff6b6b':'#51cf66';type.textContent=iv.perfect?'Perfect':'Imperfect';wrapper.appendChild(bar);group.appendChild(wrapper);group.appendChild(label);group.appendChild(type);container.appendChild(group);setTimeout(()=>{bar.style.height=(iv.loops/12*100)+'%';},100+i*150);});</script></body></html>"
