=\"bar-label\">1/12</div></div></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Minor 3rd</h3><div class=\"type\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">● Imperfect (3)</div><div class=\"count\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">12</div><div>self-loops</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:100%;background:#51cf66\"></div><div class=\"bar-label\">12/12</div></div></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Major 3rd</h3><div class=\"type\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">● Imperfect (4)</div><div class=\"count\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">12</div><div>self-loops</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:100%;background:#51cf66\"></div><div class=\"bar-label\">12/12</div></div></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Perfect 5th</h3><div class=\"type\" style=\"color:#ff6b6b\">● Perfect (7)</div><div class=\"count\" style=\"color:#ff6b6b\">1</div><div>self-loop</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:8.3%;background:#ff6b6b\"></div><div class=\"bar-label\">1/12</div></div></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Minor 6th</h3><div class=\"type\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">● Imperfect (8)</div><div class=\"count\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">12</div><div>self-loops</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:100%;background:#51cf66\"></div><div class=\"bar-label\">12/12</div></div></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Major 6th</h3><div class=\"type\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">● Imperfect (9)</div><div class=\"count\" style=\"color:#51cf66\">12</div><div>self-loops</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:100%;background:#51cf66\"></div><div class=\"bar-label\">12/12</div></div></div></div><div class=\"ratio-box\"><div>Bottleneck Ratio</div><div class=\"ratio\">12 : 1</div><div style=\"color:#888;margin-top:8px\">Imperfect : Perfect self-loops</div></div><div class=\"explanation\">A self-loop is a voice leading that preserves the interval — both voices move by the same amount. At a <strong style=\"color:#51cf66\">imperfect consonance</strong>, all 12 parallel motions are legal. At a <strong style=\"color:#ff6b6b\">perfect consonance</strong>, 11 of 12 are forbidden (only the identity survives). This 12:1 ratio is the mathematical heart of why parallel fifths and octaves are prohibited in counterpoint: perfect consonances are <em>categorical bottlenecks</em>.</div></body></html>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Voice-Swap Asymmetry on the ℤ/12ℤ Clock",
      "description": "See how the involution i ↦ −i breaks consonance, formalizing the privileged role of the bass voice.",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Voice-Swap Asymmetry</title><style>*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}body{font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0a0a1a;color:#e0e0e0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:30px;min-height:100vh}h1{font-size:1.5em;color:#fff;margin-bottom:6px}h2{font-size:.95em;font-weight:400;color:#888;margin-bottom:24px}.wrapper{display:flex;gap:30px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;align-items:center}canvas{border-radius:12px;background:#12122a;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.5)}.info-panel{background:#16163a;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;max-width:360px}.info-panel h3{color:#7af;margin-bottom:12px}.mapping{padding:8px 12px;margin:4px 0;border-radius:8px;font-size:.95em;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}.mapping.preserved{background:#1a3a1a}.mapping.broken{background:#3a1a1a;border:1px solid #ff6b6b}.arrow{color:#888;font-size:1.2em}.note{margin-top:16px;padding:12px;background:#1a1a44;border-radius:8px;font-size:.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#aaa}</style></head><body><h1>Voice-Swap Asymmetry</h1><h2>The involution i ↦ −i (mod 12) does NOT preserve consonance</h2><div class=\"wrapper\"><canvas id=\"clock\" width=\"420\" height=\"420\"></canvas><div class=\"info-panel\"><h3>The Negation Map on ℤ/12ℤ</h3><div class=\"mapping preserved\"><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">0 (Unison)</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">0 (Unison) ✓</span></div><div class=\"mapping preserved\"><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">3 (Min 3rd)</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">9 (Maj 6th) ✓</span></div><div class=\"mapping preserved\"><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">4 (Maj 3rd)</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">8 (Min 6th) ✓</span></div><div class=\"mapping broken\"><span style=\"color:#ff6b6b\">7 (Perf 5th)</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span><span style=\"color:#ff4444\">5 (Perf 4th) ✗</span></div><div class=\"mapping preserved\"><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">8 (Min 6th)</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">4 (Maj 3rd) ✓</span></div><div class=\"mapping preserved\"><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">9 (Maj 6th)</span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span><span style=\"color:#51cf66\">3 (Min 3rd) ✓</span></div><div class=\"note\"><strong style=\"color:#ff6b6b\">The break:</strong> The perfect fifth (7) maps to the perfect fourth (5), which is <em>dissonant</em> in first-species counterpoint. This asymmetry formalizes why the bass voice has a privileged role — a fifth above the bass is consonant, but a fifth below (a fourth above) is not.</div></div></div><script>const c=document.getElementById('clock'),ctx=c.getContext('2d');const W=420,H=420,cx=W/2,cy=H/2,R=160;const CONSONANT=new Set([0,3,4,7,8,9]);const PERFECT=new Set([0,7]);const NAMES=['P1/P8','m2','M2','m3','M3','P4','TT','P5','m6','M6','m7','M7'];const NEGMAP={0:0,3:9,4:8,7:5,8:4,9:3};function posOf(i){const a=-Math.PI/2+i*2*Math.PI/12;return[cx+R*Math.cos(a),cy+R*Math.sin(a)];}function draw(){ctx.clearRect(0,0,W,H);ctx.strokeStyle='#222';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(cx,cy,R,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.stroke();for(let i=0;i<12;i++){const[x,y]=posOf(i);const isCons=CONSONANT.has(i);const isPerf=PERFECT.has(i);const r=isCons?16:10;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x,y,r,0,2*Math.PI);if(isCons){if(isPerf){ctx.fillStyle='#ff6b6b';}else{ctx.fillStyle='#51cf66';}}else{ctx.fillStyle=i===5?'#ff4444':'#333';}ctx.fill();if(i===5){ctx.strokeStyle='#ff4444';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.stroke();}ctx.fillStyle='#fff';ctx.font=`bold ${isCons?12:10}px sans-serif`;ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.textBaseline='middle';ctx.fillText(i.toString(),x,y);const lr=R+30;const a=-Math.PI/2+i*2*Math.PI/12;const lx=cx+lr*Math.cos(a),ly=cy+lr*Math.sin(a);ctx.font='10px sans-serif';ctx.fillStyle=isCons?'#ccc':(i===5?'#ff6666':'#555');ctx.fillText(NAMES[i],lx,ly);}Object.entries(NEGMAP).forEach(([src,tgt])=>{src=parseInt(src);const[sx,sy]=posOf(src);const[tx,ty]=posOf(tgt);if(src===tgt&&src===0)return;const broken=!CONSONANT.has(tgt);const mx=(sx+tx)/2,my=(sy+ty)/2;const dx=tx-sx,dy=ty-sy;const dist=Math.sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy);const bulge=broken?40:25;const perpX=-dy/dist*bulge,perpY=dx/dist*bulge;const cpx=mx+perpX,cpy=my+perpY;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(sx,sy);ctx.quadraticCurveTo(cpx,cpy,tx,ty);ctx.strokeStyle=broken?'rgba(255,68,68,0.7)':'rgba(81,207,102,0.3)';ctx.lineWidth=broken?3:1.5;ctx.setLineDash(broken?[6,4]:[]);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([]);if(broken){ctx.font='bold 16px sans-serif';ctx.fillStyle='#ff4444';ctx.fillText('✗',cpx,cpy-10);}});}draw();</script></body></html>"
