12 parallel motions are legal. At a <strong style=\"color:#ff6b6b\">perfect consonance</strong>, 11 of 12 are forbidden (only the identity survives). This 12:1 ratio is the mathematical heart of why parallel fifths and octaves are prohibited in counterpoint: perfect consonances are <em>categorical bottlenecks</em>.</div></body></html>"
    },
