    {
      "title": "Catalog Impossibility & Compression",
      "description": "Explore the catalog impossibility theorem and compression limits interactively.",
      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0\"><title>Catalog & Compression</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}body{font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0a0a1a;color:#e0e0e0;padding:20px;min-height:100vh}.container{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto}h1{text-align:center;color:#50fa7b;font-size:1.5em;margin-bottom:5px}h2{text-align:center;color:#6272a4;font-size:0.9em;margin-bottom:20px;font-weight:normal}.panel{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e,#16213e);border:1px solid #44475a;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px}.panel h3{color:#ff79c6;margin-bottom:12px;font-size:1.1em}.controls{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:15px;align-items:end}.cg{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}.cg label{font-size:0.8em;color:#bd93f9}.cg input,.cg select{background:#0d1117;border:1px solid #44475a;color:#f8f8f2;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:5px;font-size:0.9em;width:70px}.result{background:#0d1117;border-radius:8px;padding:15px;font-size:0.9em;line-height:1.8}.highlight{color:#50fa7b;font-weight:bold}.warn{color:#ff5555;font-weight:bold}.bar-container{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin:8px 0}.bar{height:24px;border-radius:4px;transition:width 0.3s}.bar-label{font-size:0.8em;white-space:nowrap;min-width:120px}.theorem-box{background:#282a36;border-left:3px solid #8be9fd;padding:10px 15px;margin-top:12px;border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#8be9fd}</style></head><body><div class=\"container\"><h1>🔮 Catalog Impossibility & Compression Limits</h1><h2>Finite Cantor diagonalization in the Library of Babel</h2><div class=\"panel\"><h3>1. Catalog Impossibility (catalog_impossibility)</h3><div class=\"controls\"><div class=\"cg\"><label>A</label><input id=\"catA\" type=\"number\" value=\"2\" min=\"2\" max=\"10\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>L</label><input id=\"catL\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"10\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>D</label><input id=\"catD\" type=\"number\" value=\"2\" min=\"2\" max=\"10\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" id=\"catResult\"></div><div class=\"theorem-box\"><strong>Theorem (catalog_impossibility):</strong> For D ≥ 2 and A<sup>L</sup> ≥ 1, we have |Vol(A,L)| &lt; |CatalogScheme(A,L,D)|.<br><strong>Theorem (no_catalog_embedding):</strong> No injection f : CatalogScheme → Vol exists.<br><strong>Theorem (babel_cantor):</strong> No surjection g : Vol → CatalogScheme exists.</div></div><div class=\"panel\"><h3>2. Compression Limits (incompressible_ge_compressible)</h3><div class=\"controls\"><div class=\"cg\"><label>A</label><input id=\"compA\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"2\" max=\"6\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>L (original)</label><input id=\"compL\" type=\"number\" value=\"5\" min=\"2\" max=\"12\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>M (compressed)</label><input id=\"compM\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"11\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" id=\"compResult\"></div><div class=\"theorem-box\"><strong>Theorem (incompressible_ge_compressible):</strong> For A ≥ 2 and M &lt; L, any compression–decompression cycle loses at least as many volumes as it preserves: |{v | decompress(compress(v)) ≠ v}| ≥ |{v | decompress(compress(v)) = v}|.</div></div><div class=\"panel\"><h3>3. Periodic Structure (periodic_volume_count)</h3><div class=\"controls\"><div class=\"cg\"><label>A</label><input id=\"perA\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"6\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>L</label><input id=\"perL\" type=\"number\" value=\"12\" min=\"1\" max=\"20\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" id=\"perResult\"></div><div class=\"theorem-box\"><strong>Theorem (periodic_volume_count):</strong> For p | L, the number of p-periodic volumes is exactly A<sup>p</sup>.</div></div></div><script>function updateCatalog(){const A=Math.max(2,parseInt(document.getElementById('catA').value)||2);const L=Math.max(1,parseInt(document.getElementById('catL').value)||1);const D=Math.max(2,parseInt(document.getElementById('catD').value)||2);const vol=Math.pow(A,L);const catLog=vol*Math.log10(D);const volLog=Math.log10(vol);let html=`<div>Library size |Vol(${A}, ${L})| = ${A}<sup>${L}</sup> = <span class=\"highlight\">${vol.toLocaleString()}</span></div>`;html+=`<div>Catalog schemes |CatalogScheme| = ${D}<sup>${vol}</sup>`;if(vol<=20){html+=` = <span class=\"highlight\">${Math.pow(D,vol).toLocaleString()}</span>`}else{html+=` ≈ <span class=\"highlight\">10<sup>${catLog.toFixed(1)}</sup></span>`}html+=`</div>`;const ratio=catLog-volLog;html+=`<div style=\"margin-top:8px\">Ratio: catalogs/volumes ≈ 10<sup>${ratio.toFixed(1)}</sup> — <span class=\"warn\">${ratio>0?'catalogs overwhelmingly outnumber volumes':'error'}</span></div>`;html+=`<div class=\"bar-container\"><span class=\"bar-label\">Volumes</span><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:${Math.min(100,100*volLog/Math.max(catLog,1))}%;background:#ff79c6\"></div><span>${volLog.toFixed(1)} digits</span></div>`;html+=`<div class=\"bar-container\"><span class=\"bar-label\">Catalog Schemes</span><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:100%;background:#8be9fd\"></div><span>${catLog.toFixed(1)} digits</span></div>`;document.getElementById('catResult').innerHTML=html}function updateCompression(){const A=Math.max(2,parseInt(document.getElementById('compA').value)||2);const L=Math.max(2,parseInt(document.getElementById('compL').value)||2);let M=Math.max(1,parseInt(document.getElementById('compM').value)||1);if(M>=L)M=L-1;const volL=Math.pow(A,L);const volM=Math.pow(A,M);const maxRecoverable=volM;const minLost=volL-volM;const pctRecoverable=(maxRecoverable/volL*100);const pctLost=(minLost/volL*100);let html=`<div>Original library: A<sup>${L}</sup> = <span class=\"highlight\">${volL.toLocaleString()}</span> volumes</div>`;html+=`<div>Compressed space: A<sup>${M}</sup> = <span class=\"highlight\">${volM.toLocaleString()}</span> possible compressed forms</div>`;html+=`<div style=\"margin-top:8px\">Maximum recoverable: ≤ <span class=\"highlight\">${maxRecoverable.toLocaleString()}</span> (${pctRecoverable.toFixed(2)}%)</div>`;html+=`<div>Minimum lost: ≥ <span class=\"warn\">${minLost.toLocaleString()}</span> (${pctLost.toFixed(2)}%)</div>`;html+=`<div style=\"margin-top:8px\">Lost ≥ Recoverable? <span class=\"${minLost>=maxRecoverable?'highlight':'warn'}\">${minLost>=maxRecoverable?'✓ YES':'✗ NO (need M < L and A ≥ 2)'}</span></div>`;html+=`<div class=\"bar-container\"><span class=\"bar-label\">Recoverable</span><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:${Math.max(1,pctRecoverable)}%;background:#50fa7b\"></div><span>${pctRecoverable.toFixed(1)}%</span></div>`;html+=`<div class=\"bar-container\"><span class=\"bar-label\">Lost forever</span><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:${Math.max(1,pctLost)}%;background:#ff5555\"></div><span>${pctLost.toFixed(1)}%</span></div>`;document.getElementById('compResult').innerHTML=html}function updatePeriodic(){const A=Math.max(1,parseInt(document.getElementById('perA').value)||1);const L=Math.max(1,parseInt(document.getElementById('perL').value)||1);const libSize=Math.pow(A,L);let html=`<div>Library: A<sup>${L}</sup> = ${libSize>1e15?'10<sup>'+Math.log10(libSize).toFixed(1)+'</sup>':libSize.toLocaleString()} volumes</div>`;html+=`<div style=\"margin-top:8px\">Periodic subsets (p divides ${L}):</div>`;let found=false;for(let p=1;p<=L;p++){if(L%p!==0)continue;found=true;const count=Math.pow(A,p);const frac=count/libSize;const pctW=Math.max(1,Math.log10(count+1)/Math.log10(libSize+1)*100);html+=`<div class=\"bar-container\"><span class=\"bar-label\">p=${p}: A<sup>${p}</sup>=${count>1e12?'10^'+Math.log10(count).toFixed(1):count.toLocaleString()}</span><div class=\"bar\" style=\"width:${pctW}%;background:hsl(${p*30},70%,50%)\"></div><span>${(frac*100).toFixed(frac<0.01?4:2)}%</span></div>`}document.getElementById('perResult').innerHTML=html}['catA','catL','catD'].forEach(id=>document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input',updateCatalog));['compA','compL','compM'].forEach(id=>document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input',updateCompression));['perA','perL'].forEach(id=>document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input',updatePeriodic));updateCatalog();updateCompression();updatePeriodic()</script></body></html>"
    }
  ]
